code (origin/nightly):
  - "Default input transport is session_socket (runtime_input_gateway.py:20, chat_http_controller.py:61; cd32b97 2026-09-03)."
  - "write_session_socket is always wired to _CLAUDE_SESSION_SOCKET.send (ciel_runtime.py:4433)."
  - "Codex launches return at runtime_launch.py:328 before configure_session_socket (only in run_claude_process, line 625), so the socket target stays empty and send() returns False with INFO claude_session_socket_deferred reason=target_unconfigured (claude_session_socket.py:100-103)."
  - "channel_pending_injection.py: a session_socket request skips the active_turn/active_tool_call deferral (line 202); after send() returns False the tty fallback runs only when no turn/tool call is active (line 340); otherwise submitted stays False and the batch is failed prompt_not_submitted (line 370) (60846f9 2026-09-01). The failure is terminal but no longer blocks: later scans log channel_stdin_proxy_blocked ... action=skipped and continue past it (2297021 2026-09-22). Correction: the first report to the user said it blocks later messages; that was wrong."
  - "Batching: session_socket requests are collected into one prompt up to wake_batch_limit (CIEL_RUNTIME_CHANNEL_WAKE_BATCH_LIMIT, default 8; 4cccb27 2026-09-23, comment 'everything deferred behind a busy turn goes in together'). A message whose earlier wake is still pending/queued stops the scan (channel_stdin_proxy_waiting_for_turn_completion) so later messages accumulate. Celly: 613-617 arrived in Codex as one input '5 new messages' at 15:54:55, right after the 15:51:31-15:54:55 compaction turn."
