correction_windows_outer_deferral: "channel_pending_poll.py (cf41ddb): while services.active() is true the poll scans only if session_socket_ready(); that is False for Codex (default lambda), so on a Codex ConPTY session nothing is typed mid-turn and the inner busy+session_socket failure seen in the harness is not reached in normal flow. E2E evidence/e2e-codex-1790897969 (codex 0.160.0, 45 s slow turn): 'channel_windows_console_deferred cursor=1 reason=active_turn' during the turn, then message 2 (default session_socket) 'session_socket_submit_failed fallback=tty' at the turn end, submit_confirmed attempt=1, replied. The earlier statement that Codex messages fail because the socket path skips the busy deferral is withdrawn for Windows ConPTY sessions."
